# ADR-003: Salting Strategy for Region-Based Skew

**Date:** 2026-06-24
**Status:** Accepted

## Context
orders.region is heavily skewed — IN-SOUTH represents ~70% 
of rows. GroupBy on region causes one partition to process 
70% of data while others sit idle.

## Decision
Apply salting to region column before aggregation:
1. Add random salt (0 to SALT_COUNT-1) to skewed key
2. Partial aggregate on salted key
3. Final aggregate after removing salt

## SALT_COUNT Sizing
Not based on number of distinct keys.
Based on: (skewed key row count) ÷ (target rows per partition)
Current: 70,000 IN-SOUTH rows, target ~10,000/partition
SALT_COUNT = 7-8 for even distribution

## Measured Impact
At 100K rows (Colab, 2 cores): 24.6% improvement
Expected at production scale (50+ workers): 80-90%+ improvement
Benefit scales with cluster size — limited demonstration in Colab

## Consequences
✅ Prevents single-worker bottleneck on skewed keys
✅ Scales with cluster size — bigger benefit at production scale
❌ Adds complexity (two-phase aggregation instead of one)
❌ Requires monitoring — skew distribution can shift over time
⏳ Re-evaluate SALT_COUNT if regional distribution changes
